<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Additional Evaluation Details</h3>

<section id="A1.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.6.1 </span>Grounding</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In grounding evaluations (Table <a href="#A1.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ A.6.1 Grounding ‣ A.6 Additional Evaluation Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ GUIrilla: A Scalable Framework for Automated Desktop UI Exploration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), <span id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GUIrilla-See</span> (7B) achieved the highest overall accuracy at 75.59%. <span id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GUIrilla-See</span> (7B) showed particularly strong results on buttons, input fields, and "Other" elements such as icons and links, demonstrating robust performance across varied UI components. Interestingly, UGround shows marginal advantages in menu-heavy tasks, and we found their data to contain 400× more menu samples, reflecting the limits of scale without functional task diversity.</p>
</div>
